<title>JAPAN: Nintendo to launch 64-bit game machine in Europe.</title>
<headline>Nintendo to launch 64-bit game machine in Europe.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nintendo Co Ltd said on Tuesday it plans to start selling its new 64-bit game machine &quot;Nintendo64&quot; in Europe on March 1, 1997.  </p>
<p>The game machine will sell in Germany for 399 marks, a Nintendo spokesman said. He did not give prices for other countries or an estimate for European sales of the machine.</p>
<p>Nintendo introduced its newest game machine in Japan on June 23 and will launch it in the United States on September 29.</p>
</text>
